      "rollRad": 0.0,
      "yfovRad": 0.47108996144172666,
      "sensorHeightMm": 24.0,
      "clipStartM": 7.045297083802107,
      "clipEndM": 9.339567637329692,
      "derivation": "The framing rule of src/gltf/Framing.h, quoted so the runner can refuse a mismatch rather than trust it. World bounds [-0.3120085895061493, 0.0110623212531209, -0.3619171977043152] to [0.8149782419204712, 1.8746249675750732, 0.35968679189682007], so centre = [0.25148482620716095, 0.9428436444140971, -0.0011152029037475586] and radius = 1.1471352767637921 m. yfov = 2*atan(12/50) from a 50 mm lens on a 24 mm sensor height at sensor_fit VERTICAL. distance = radius / sin(yfov/2) / 0.6 = 8.192432360565899, and the eye is centre + (cos20*cos35, sin20, cos20*sin35) * distance. clipStart is distance - radius and clipEnd is distance + radius.",
      "note": "The glTF carries no camera, so the framing rule supplies one. Roll is 0 because the rule sets it: a roll chosen here and nowhere else would make this subject's placement a second determination competing with the rule."
    },
    "light": {
      "kind": "none",
      "note": "The material emits, so nothing has to arrive for the picture to exist."
    },
    "world": {
      "kind": "uniform",
      "colourLinear": [
        1.0,
        1.0,
        1.0
      ],
      "strength": 0.0,
      "note": "Declared and zero rather than left factory, so the picture is a function of this manifest and not of a Blender default."
    },
    "material": {
      "source": "manifest",
      "kind": "emission-by-material-index",
      "note": "Emission, one colour per glTF material, from a RULE with no free parameter rather than from a table: colour[c] = 0.15 + 0.70 * frac(index * step[c]). A table names materials and is right while a subject draws a handful; past that it is a transcription of the file. The rule takes no parameter, so a manifest cannot tune a colour to make a case pass (board:1362)."
    }
  },
