        "exposure": 0.0,
        "gamma": 1.0
      },
      "exrCodec": "ZIP",
      "note": "The same recipe with the sampler's seed moved. At one sample per pixel of a deterministic emission there is nothing for a seed to change, so any pixel that moves between these two renders is the oracle's own noise rather than a disagreement with us -- which is what makes this the instrument floor instead of an assumption about it."
    }
  },
  "notes": "A coverage case. Its shading -- textures, metallic-roughness, any extension it declares -- is NOT what this decides; board:1363 records why no case takes the shading arm yet. THE LIGHTS THE FILE DECLARES ARE NOT READ BY THIS CASE and that is stated rather than implied: the manifest declares no light and the material emits, so what is decided is where the three bodies are. The lamp's own illumination is a shading question.",
